                "entry_id": "3126abb3-420f-35fd-92d2-925a872c27ba",
                "word": "afrothérien",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e5119bdf-c0c2-43fc-a06f-f5917c6c92d4",
                        "entry_id": "3126abb3-420f-35fd-92d2-925a872c27ba",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "afrothériens"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a59582e3-3a46-377e-819a-a349f5320d03",
                        "entry_id": "3126abb3-420f-35fd-92d2-925a872c27ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mammifère placentaire de l’ordre des Afrotheria, c’est-à-dire dont l’origine se situe en Afrique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9202eec7-e3ee-4116-933f-2e84bf772f98",
                                "sense_id": "a59582e3-3a46-377e-819a-a349f5320d03",
                                "text": "Les afrosoricides (tenrécidés, chrysochloridés, potamogalidés), inféodés à l’Afrique et Madagascar, sont des afrothériens, tandis que les eulipotyphles sont des laurasiathériens."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f277d802-e211-4994-999a-0cf733bbf40e",
                                "sense_id": "a59582e3-3a46-377e-819a-a349f5320d03",
                                "text": "Les Afrothériens englobent sept classes de mammifères très différents qui vont du plus gros, l'éléphant, au presque plus petit, la taupe dorée."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "52c9d72e-9cba-41fc-ac35-e3a52c48d50b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3126abb3-420f-35fd-92d2-925a872c27ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "a59582e3-3a46-377e-819a-a349f5320d03",
                        "target_lang_word": "afrothere",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "afrothere",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "754a94aa-2dcd-3edd-8209-516379a02c68",
                                        "entry_id": "d3c7d546-24b1-3c7f-b5b3-5947676206d8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An afrotherian."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87a69ab0-90bd-4df7-8b76-a811611903d2",
                                                "sense_id": "754a94aa-2dcd-3edd-8209-516379a02c68",
                                                "text": "Golden moles and tenrecs seem to be related to each other, and most modern authorities place them within the afrotheres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1a40733-ce41-4aa7-9bab-669c837076aa",
                                                "sense_id": "754a94aa-2dcd-3edd-8209-516379a02c68",
                                                "text": "In the absence of a comprehensive fossil record for stem members of crown Afrotheria, most high-level phylogenetic analyses have been based primarily on the morphology of extant afrotheres[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "323a9283-c02d-47c5-ad51-e177581aa5aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "3126abb3-420f-35fd-92d2-925a872c27ba",
                        "source_sense_id": "a59582e3-3a46-377e-819a-a349f5320d03",
                        "target_lang_word": "afrotherian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "afrotherian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eaeb7836-0620-3ec4-a91b-efe8804b4cc4",
                                        "entry_id": "e7304c43-c4df-3b19-841b-39c22260786a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belonging or pertaining to the superorder Afrotheria, which includes the elephants, aardvarks, golden moles, tenrecs, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38927a89-aa0d-44b1-99ef-6dcdd67d17e9",
                                                "sense_id": "eaeb7836-0620-3ec4-a91b-efe8804b4cc4",
                                                "text": "Although the monophyly of Afrotheria is well supported by recent molecular studies, the interrelationships within afrotherian mammals remain unclarified."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecfb9bf5-761b-4d24-aacf-33ac2be11890",
                                                "sense_id": "eaeb7836-0620-3ec4-a91b-efe8804b4cc4",
                                                "text": "Just as molecular evidence from living mammals would predict, the African fossil record documents the presence of several afrotherian groups by early or middle Eocene time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "afrotherian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88fd999e-3745-308d-9c46-04e647d72fca",
                                        "entry_id": "df6c9746-d001-3efd-b0a0-a7ae54050f79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A placental that belongs to the superorder Afrotheria, such as an elephant, aardvark, golden mole, tenrec, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2071d152-e55c-4fbd-a234-ea165b6baa90",
                                                "sense_id": "88fd999e-3745-308d-9c46-04e647d72fca",
                                                "text": "As their name implies, afrotherians putatively represent a radiation of placentals rooted in the African continent and nearby island of Madagascar."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "798e40ce-79af-4e3a-a9d0-ddaec7e4334b",
                                                "sense_id": "88fd999e-3745-308d-9c46-04e647d72fca",
                                                "text": "Alternatively, the afrotherians may have originated in Europe, and an elephant-shrew like creature crossed into Africa and gave rise to the great diversity of afrotherians—from elephants to golden moles—that inhabit the continent today."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce372a9a-f9a2-43a3-acb3-f55cc261bb87",
